Subject: [PATCH] viogpu3d: map the source of a present copy in Present, and never fail Patch

In a Venus context the driver copies a Blt present from a blob into a GDI
surface. The mapping of the two surfaces was made in Present only when
both allocations were resident or mapped already. Otherwise it was left to
Patch, which has no way to refuse one present: upstream's comment there
says that Windows answers a failure of DxgkDdiPatch with bugcheck 0x119.

Whether the source blob maps is decided by the private data of
D3DKMTCreateAllocation, which the calling program writes: a blob without
VIRTGPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_MAPPABLE, a size the shared memory does not hold. So
a standard user can have the driver accept a present that it cannot carry
out: an allocation of Venus device memory with BlobFlags 0, presented
while Windows still pages it in. On Windows 11 (26100) the scheduler stops
that DMA buffer before it calls DxgkDdiPatch ("allocation has not been
fully committed prior to being scheduled") and puts the device of the
program into its error state, so the guest stays up. The driver must not
depend on that.

Three changes:

- A blob source without the mappable flag is refused when the copy is
  staged, with STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED. Before, only a blob destination asked
  for the flag.
- Present maps the source blob in every case. A blob's mapping does not
  depend on residency, and a failure fails that Present only. The mapping
  stays with the allocation, so Patch finds it made. The mapping of a GDI
  destination still waits for Patch when the destination is not resident.
- Patch returns success when its mapping fails. The command then has no
  mappings, and Run() skips the copy, logs it and retires the DMA buffer
  as the NOP it holds: one frame of one window is not copied. This is for
  what Present cannot see, a mapping lost to a device reset between the
  two calls.

The two rules are in viogpu_blt_map.h, a header with no include:
tests/kmd/blt_map_test.cpp of the package compiles it on the build host.

Card #756, finding F8 of the win3d driver review. docs/acceptance/C756.md
has the proof.
---
diff --git a/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_blt_map.h b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_blt_map.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c38962c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/viogpu/viogpu3d/viogpu_blt_map.h
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+/*
+ * Where the copy of a Blt present gets its mappings.
+ *
+ * In a Venus context the driver copies a Blt present from a blob (a Venus
+ * image) into a GDI surface or another blob. The copy needs a kernel
+ * mapping of both. Present can refuse the call when a mapping fails.
+ * Patch cannot: it has no status that Windows takes for "refuse this one
+ * present". Whether a blob can be mapped depends on values that the
+ * calling program wrote into the private data of D3DKMTCreateAllocation
+ * (BlobMem, BlobFlags, BlobId, Size), so no mapping of a blob may wait for
+ * Patch.
+ *
+ * This header includes nothing and uses no kernel type, so that a test
+ * program on the build host can compile it.
+ */
+#pragma once
+
+/* VIRTIO_GPU_BLOB_FLAG_USE_MAPPABLE */
+#define VIOGPU_BLT_BLOB_FLAG_MAPPABLE 0x0001u
+
+/* Which surfaces the copy takes. The source is a mappable blob. The
+ * destination is a GDI surface or, for Desktop Duplication, a second
+ * mappable blob. */
+static inline int VioGpuBltSurfacesSupported(int src_is_blob, unsigned int src_blob_flags, int dst_is_blob,
+                                             unsigned int dst_blob_flags)
+{
+    if (!src_is_blob || !(src_blob_flags & VIOGPU_BLT_BLOB_FLAG_MAPPABLE))
+    {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return !dst_is_blob || (dst_blob_flags & VIOGPU_BLT_BLOB_FLAG_MAPPABLE) != 0;
+}
+
+/* What Present maps before it accepts the call. */
+#define VIOGPU_BLT_PRESENT_MAP_SOURCE 1 /* the source blob, to prove that it maps */
+#define VIOGPU_BLT_PRESENT_MAP_BOTH   2 /* both, and the command keeps the mappings */
+
+/* A blob's mapping does not depend on residency, so the source is mapped
+ * in every Present. A GDI destination has a mapping only while it is
+ * resident: Present maps it when Windows may skip Patch (both allocations
+ * resident) or when both have a mapping already, and leaves it to Patch
+ * otherwise. Patch runs with the destination paged in. */
+static inline int VioGpuBltPresentMap(int dst_is_blob, int both_resident, int both_mapped)
+{
+    return (dst_is_blob || both_resident || both_mapped) ? VIOGPU_BLT_PRESENT_MAP_BOTH : VIOGPU_BLT_PRESENT_MAP_SOURCE;
+}
